OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30510
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785338294
OL,3,CNorwegian teenager travelled to the UK
OL,4,Cto carry out a hit for Iran-backed gang
OL,6,FDespite having supportive parents, his
OL,7,Flife went downhill after getting
OL,8,Fhooked on drugs and he was placed in
OL,9,Frehab and a care home, he said.
OL,11,FHe initially agreed to the plan to
OL,12,Fshoot someone in England for money to
OL,13,Fpay for drugs, thinking it was a
OL,14,F"joke" or a "scam", he said.
OL,16,FAfter realising he was in a "pickle"
OL,17,Fwith the Swedish Foxtrot gang, Natland
OL,18,Fsaid he planned to shoot himself in
OL,19,Fthe foot to get out of it, he said.
OL,26,@vD@AOUvD@FO]vD@MOUvD@RO]xD@]OUxD@dO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30511
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785338294
OL,3,CNorwegian teenager travelled to the UK
OL,4,Cto carry out a hit for Iran-backed gang
OL,6,FHe told jurors: "I was going to look
OL,7,Flike an idiot but desperate times call
OL,8,Ffor desperate measures. Faced with the
OL,9,Falternative of being shot in the head,
OL,10,FI thought being shot in the foot is
OL,11,Fbetter, yeah."
OL,13,FUnder cross-examination, he agreed
OL,14,Fthat he had lied repeatedly in his
OL,15,Fwritten account of what happened and
OL,16,Fnever once mentioned being scared
OL,17,Fbefore giving evidence at his trial.
OL,26,@nD@QOUsD@NO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30512
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785338294
OL,3,CNorwegian teenager travelled to the UK
OL,4,Cto carry out a hit for Iran-backed gang
OL,6,FProsecutor Alistair Richardson told
OL,7,Fjurors: "The reality is the defendant
OL,8,Fis a troubled but dangerous young man.
OL,9,FA young man who agreed to kill in a
OL,10,Fforeign country for money."
OL,12,FThe true identity and whereabouts of
OL,13,FNatland's English-speaking controller,
OL,14,FAgent 47, remain unknown.
OL,16,FFrank Ferguson, from the Crown
OL,17,FProsecution Service, said: "This case
OL,18,Fshows how organised crime networks
OL,19,Foperate across borders and exploit
OL,20,Fyoung people to carry out serious
OL,21,Fviolence.
OL,26,@oD@IOUrD@[O]yD@\OU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30513
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785338294
OL,3,CNorwegian teenager travelled to the UK
OL,4,Cto carry out a hit for Iran-backed gang
OL,6,F"This conviction sends a clear
OL,7,Fmessage: if you come to this country
OL,8,Fto commit serious violence on behalf
OL,9,Fof organised criminals, you will be
OL,10,Fcaught and we will make sure you are
OL,11,Fbrought to justice."
